<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Nan Ya May sales edge higher.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Nan Ya May sales edge higher.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nan Ya Plastics Corp, Taiwan's largest industrial enterprise, said on Thursday its May sales edged 4.9 percent higher to T$8.118 billion from May 1996.</p>
<p>The firm's combined January-May sales rose 7.9 percent to T$38.174 billion from the same period a year ago, a company statement said.</p>
<p>The statement did not give profit figures.</p>
<p>Nan Ya has a sales target of T$94.921 billion for 1997.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
